{
  "summary": "Excludes expired and revoked GPG signatures from counting toward the binary verification quorum in `contrib/verify-binaries/verify.py` by default. Adds an `--allow-expired` CLI flag and `BINVERIFY_ALLOW_EXPIRED` environment variable to permit expired keys when verifying older releases, while keeping revoked signatures unconditionally excluded. Adds parsing for `KEYREVOKED` status records, ensures revocation takes precedence over expiration, and reports expired signatures in a dedicated `expired_sigs` JSON field.",
  "problem": "`contrib/verify-binaries/verify.py` treats signatures from expired or revoked keys as valid signatures satisfying `--min-good-sigs`. A verification run can therefore pass and report binaries as verified even if all supplied signatures come from compromised or defunct keys.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This was found and disclosed responsibly by the Red Team 🟥.'",
    "PR description: 'The binary verifier counts signatures from expired and revoked keys toward `--min-good-sigs`. Enough of these signatures can satisfy the threshold without any active signing key, and they are returned as good signatures.'"
  ],
