  "changed_since_previous": "Added explicit handling for GnuPG's `KEYREVOKED` status tag to prioritize revocation over expiration when both are reported, extracted `build_parser()` to facilitate testing, and added unit tests mocking GnuPG outputs across multiple environment and argument combinations.",
  "card": "Excludes expired and revoked GPG signatures from counting toward the binary verification threshold in contrib/verify-binaries/verify.py by default. Previously, release binary verification could succeed using only expired or revoked keys, an issue disclosed responsibly by the Red Team. To accommodate historical releases signed by keys that have since expired, an --allow-expired flag allows expired keys to count toward the threshold while revoked keys remain strictly excluded. Expired signatures are emitted separately in JSON output, and revocation status is given precedence over expiration.",
